cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, its computational workflow, datasets, results, or derived figures, please cite the associated research work and this repository."

title: "TP53 Evolutionary Conservation Across Mammals"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible comparative bioinformatics workflow investigating evolutionary
  conservation and functional constraint at recurrent human TP53 cancer
  mutation hotspots across mammalian species. The repository integrates
  curated protein sequences, multiple sequence alignment, residue-level
  conservation analysis, hotspot mapping, cancer mutation information,
  permutation-based statistical analysis, phylogenetic reconstruction,
  structural context, and reproducible research documentation.

